            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0691" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./326:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-14T17:00:00-06:00">March 14, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Your telegram No. 17 of February 28, 7 p.m. and my despatch No. 814 of
                    February 23rd.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d349-f1"/> On March 12th the National
                    Congress demanded that the Pan American Airways contract be reported out of
                    committee. At the request of the local representative of the company and in
                    order to prevent a vote on the measure, the Executive at once ordered the
                    withdrawal of the contract for modification. Yesterday the Congress decided to
                    ignore the order of the Executive and now it is reported that the contract was
                    disapproved unanimously this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
